   "pdfjsText": "Masters of Education (COQP15)\nNote:\ni. The Question Paper will have 75 questions.\nii. All questions will be based on Subject-Specific Knowledge.\niii. All questions are compulsory.\niv. The Questions will be Bilingual (English/Hindi).\nMasters of Education (COQP15)\nUnit I: Basics of Education\nMeaning and nature of Education:\n• Modes of Education- Formal, Non-formal, Open and MOOCS.\n• Aims of Education\n• Philosophy and Education\n• Meaning and Scope of Philosophy\n• Functions of Philosophy\n• Relationship between Education and Philosophy\n• Significance of Philosophy of Education\nSchools of Philosophy:\n• Naturalism\n• Idealism\n• Pragmatism\n• Vedant\n• Buddhism\n• Jainism\nEducational Thinkers: Swami Vivekananda, M.K Gandhi, Tagore, Allamah, Iqbal, John Dewey, J.J\nRousseau.\nUnit II\nIndian Society and Education:\n• Education as a sub-system of Indian Society\n• Education and relationship with Indian Social Structure\nSchool as a Social Unit:\n• Democracy in School life, Social Change, Social Stratification, Social Mobility\n• Culture and Education\nUnit III: Psychological Perspectives of Education\nNature & Meaning of Educational Psychology\n• Nature, Meaning and functions of Educational Psychology\nLearning & Motivation:\n• Concept of learning\n• Factors of influencing learning – Personal & Environmental\n• Transfer of Learning\n• Concept of Motivation and its types\nTechniques of enhancing learner’s motivation\n• S‐R Theory of Learning (Thorndike)\n• Classical conditioning (Pavlov)\n• Operant Conditioning\n• Theory of learning (Skinner) and Gestalt Theory of Learning (Kohler et al)\n• Cognitive theory (Piaget)\n• Social Development Theory (Vygotsky)\nBehaviorism\n• Constructivism and Eclectic approach\n2",
   "popplerText": "                                      Masters of Education (COQP15)\r\n\r\nNote:\r\n\r\n   i. The Question Paper will have 75 questions.\r\n\r\n  ii. All questions will be based on Subject-Specific Knowledge.\r\n\r\n  iii. All questions are compulsory.\r\n\r\n  iv. The Questions will be Bilingual (English/Hindi).\r\n\r\n                    Masters of Education (COQP15)\r\n\r\n                                               Unit I: Basics of Education\r\nMeaning and nature of Education:\r\n • Modes of Education- Formal, Non-formal, Open and MOOCS.\r\n • Aims of Education\r\n • Philosophy and Education\r\n • Meaning and Scope of Philosophy\r\n • Functions of Philosophy\r\n • Relationship between Education and Philosophy\r\n • Significance of Philosophy of Education\r\n\r\nSchools of Philosophy:\r\n • Naturalism\r\n • Idealism\r\n • Pragmatism\r\n • Vedant\r\n • Buddhism\r\n • Jainism\r\nEducational Thinkers: Swami Vivekananda, M.K Gandhi, Tagore, Allamah, Iqbal, John Dewey, J.J\r\n\r\n                              Rousseau.\r\n                                                          Unit II\r\n\r\nIndian Society and Education:\r\n • Education as a sub-system of Indian Society\r\n • Education and relationship with Indian Social Structure\r\nSchool as a Social Unit:\r\n • Democracy in School life, Social Change, Social Stratification, Social Mobility\r\n • Culture and Education\r\n\r\n                                Unit III: Psychological Perspectives of Education\r\n\r\nNature & Meaning of Educational Psychology\r\n • Nature, Meaning and functions of Educational Psychology\r\n\r\nLearning & Motivation:\r\n • Concept of learning\r\n • Factors of influencing learning – Personal & Environmental\r\n • Transfer of Learning\r\n • Concept of Motivation and its types\r\n\r\nTechniques of enhancing learner’s motivation\r\n • S‐R Theory of Learning (Thorndike)\r\n • Classical conditioning (Pavlov)\r\n • Operant Conditioning\r\n • Theory of learning (Skinner) and Gestalt Theory of Learning (Kohler et al)\r\n • Cognitive theory (Piaget)\r\n • Social Development Theory (Vygotsky)\r\n\r\nBehaviorism\r\n • Constructivism and Eclectic approach\r\n\r\n                                                                  2\r\n\f",
